<idea-plugin>
    <id>dev.sort.clickhouse-intellij-plugin</id>
    <name>SQL Dialect for ClickHouse</name>
    <vendor url="https://sort.dev" email="jayson@sort.dev">Sortdev SRL</vendor>
    <description><![CDATA[
        <p>A fuller <b>ClickHouse SQL dialect</b> for DataGrip and IntelliJ IDEA Ultimate. Your SQL is
        checked by your own ClickHouse server's parser, and completion follows the functions your
        server actually has. Compatible with the 2026.1 through 2026.3 IDE lines.</p>

        <ul>
            <li><b>Checked by your ClickHouse server.</b> While your data source is connected, the
                server's own parser checks each statement. It only parses: nothing runs and no data
                is read. When the server accepts a statement, local false errors go away. Local
                checks still apply when the server is unreachable</li>
            <li><b>More ClickHouse syntax than the built-in dialect.</b> Table functions in
                <code>FROM</code>, <code>JOIN</code>, <code>DESCRIBE</code> and <code>INSERT</code>,
                <code>EXISTS</code> and <code>ALL</code>/<code>ANY</code> predicates,
                <code>INSERT INTO FUNCTION</code> exports, and raw <code>FORMAT</code> data</li>
            <li><b>Completion from your server.</b> Function names are read from the connected
                server's system catalog and merged with bundled ClickHouse metadata, so completion
                and quick documentation match the version you run. <i>Refresh ClickHouse Catalog</i>
                (editor right-click) reloads them on demand</li>
            <li><b>Table function arguments</b> complete and resolve without falling back to
                unrelated table names</li>
            <li><b>Automatic targeted introspection.</b> Reference a schema that hasn't been
                introspected yet and the plugin introspects just that schema in the background</li>
            <li><b>ClickHouse PIPE (optional).</b> Write <code>FROM t |&gt; WHERE ... |&gt; SELECT ...</code>
                and run it as ClickHouse SQL, with stage completion, generated-SQL preview and
                run-to-stage. Enable it under <b>Settings &rarr; Tools &rarr; Database &rarr; ClickHouse PIPE</b>.
                Disabled by default; no SQL Transpiler plugin installation is required</li>
            <li>Ready-to-use <b>ClickHouse (sort.dev)</b> data source on ClickHouse's official JDBC
                driver (default HTTP port 8123), which selects the dialect for its consoles
                automatically. The database tree, DDL and object sources come from the IDE's
                built-in ClickHouse support</li>
        </ul>

        <p><i>This is an independent, community plugin developed by Sortdev SRL. It is not affiliated
        with, endorsed by, or sponsored by ClickHouse, Inc. "ClickHouse" is a registered trademark of
        ClickHouse, Inc., used here only to identify the database this plugin supports.</i></p>

        <p>Source, issues and documentation:
        <a href="https://github.com/sort-dev/clickhouse-intellij-plugin">github.com/sort-dev/clickhouse-intellij-plugin</a></p>
    ]]></description>
    <change-notes><![CDATA[
        <h3>0.2.1</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Engine errors for this dialect's blocks in SQL Transpiler <code>.bsql</code> scratches, and its completion and catalog features resolve against the block's own <code>using=</code> connection (SQL IntelliJ support 0.2.2).</li>
            <li>A user-facing README and plugin description with a non-affiliation notice.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>0.2.0</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Update to SQL IntelliJ support 0.2.1 without the unused generic JDBC adapter.</li>
            <li>Reduce factory delegation to the stock factory's concrete methods.</li>
            <li>Preserve native connection handling, server-object forwarding and editing behavior.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>0.1.1</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Adopt released Brikk SQL 0.20.0, SQL IDE support 0.2.0 and Kotlin IntelliJ helper 0.3.0.</li>
            <li>Preserve streaming cancellation for ClickHouse (sort.dev) consoles with JDBC 0.10.0. JDBC 0.9.8 session-lock cancellation remains unresolved.</li>
            <li>Hide inapplicable PIPE popup menus and place PIPE settings under Tools / Database.</li>
            <li>Property key/value completion remains disabled.</li>
        </ul>
    ]]></change-notes>
    <depends>com.intellij.modules.platform</depends>
    <depends>com.intellij.database</depends>
    <depends optional="true" config-file="clickhouse-kotlin.xml">org.jetbrains.kotlin</depends>
    <depends optional="true" config-file="clickhouse-bsql.xml">dev.sort.sql-transpiler-intellij-plugin</depends>
    <extensionPoints>
        <extensionPoint qualifiedName="dev.sort.clickhouse.relationFacts" interface="dev.brikk.house.sql.intellij.relation.ExternalRelationFacts" dynamic="true"/>
        <extensionPoint qualifiedName="dev.sort.clickhouse.inspectionRule" interface="dev.sort.clickhouse.brikk.ClickHouseInspectionRule" dynamic="true"/>
    </extensionPoints>
    <extensions defaultExtensionNs="org.jetbrains.kotlin">
        <supportsKotlinPluginMode supportsK2="true" supportsK1="false"/>
    </extensions>
    <extensions defaultExtensionNs="com.intellij">
        <sql.dialect dbms="CLICKHOUSE_BRIKK" implementationClass="dev.sort.clickhouse.sql.ClickHouseDialect" order="first"/>
        <lang.parserDefinition language="ClickHouseSQL" implementationClass="dev.sort.clickhouse.sql.ClickHouseParserDefinition"/>
        <lang.documentationProvider language="ClickHouseSQL" order="first" implementationClass="dev.brikk.house.sql.intellij.docs.SqlEngineDocumentationProvider"/>
        <lang.syntaxHighlighterFactory language="ClickHouseSQL" implementationClass="dev.sort.clickhouse.sql.ClickHouseSyntaxHighlighterFactory"/>
        <lang.commenter language="ClickHouseSQL" implementationClass="com.intellij.database.sql.common.core.psi.impl.support.SqlNestedCommenter"/>
        <lang.quoteHandler language="ClickHouseSQL" implementationClass="dev.sort.clickhouse.sql.ClickHouseQuoteHandler"/>
        <externalAnnotator language="ClickHouseSQL" implementationClass="dev.sort.clickhouse.validation.ClickHouseNativeErrorAnnotator"/>
        <highlightErrorFilter implementation="dev.sort.clickhouse.sql.ClickHouseSubstrateErrorFilter"/>
        <highlightErrorFilter implementation="dev.sort.clickhouse.brikk.ClickHousePlaceholderErrorFilter"/>
        <database.runConsoleAvailable implementation="dev.sort.clickhouse.brikk.ClickHouseRunConsoleVeto"/>
        <sql.resolveExtension implementation="dev.sort.clickhouse.brikk.ClickHouseRelationResolveExtension"/>
        <sql.resolveExtension implementation="dev.sort.clickhouse.sql.ClickHouseTableFunctionResolveExtension"/>
        <sql.resolveExtension implementation="dev.sort.clickhouse.sql.ClickHouseScalarFunctionResolveExtension"/>
        <sql.inspectionSuppressorDelegate implementation="dev.sort.clickhouse.brikk.ClickHouseRelationInspectionSuppressor"/>
        <completion.contributor language="ClickHouseSQL" implementationClass="dev.sort.clickhouse.brikk.ClickHouseRelationCompletionContributor" order="first, before clickhouse.metadata"/>
        <gotoDeclarationHandler implementation="dev.sort.clickhouse.brikk.ClickHouseRelationGotoDeclarationHandler"/>
        <annotator language="ClickHouseSQL" implementationClass="dev.sort.clickhouse.brikk.ClickHouseRelationAnnotator"/>
        <annotator language="ClickHouseSQL" implementationClass="dev.sort.clickhouse.sql.ClickHouseMaskedSpanAnnotator"/>
        <completion.contributor language="ClickHouseSQL" implementationClass="dev.sort.clickhouse.sql.ClickHouseCompletionContributor" id="clickhouse.metadata" order="first"/>
        <completion.contributor language="ClickHouseSQL" implementationClass="dev.sort.clickhouse.sql.ClickHouseTableFunctionArgumentCompletion" order="first, before clickhouse.metadata"/>
        <completion.confidence language="ClickHouseSQL" implementationClass="dev.sort.clickhouse.sql.ClickHouseCompletionConfidence" order="first"/>
        <completion.contributor language="ClickHouseSQL" implementationClass="dev.sort.clickhouse.pipe.ClickHouseStageCompletion" order="first, before clickhouse.metadata"/>
        <completion.contributor language="ClickHouseSQL" implementationClass="dev.sort.clickhouse.catalog.ClickHouseQualifiedPathIntrospectContributor" order="first, before clickhouse.metadata"/>
        <annotator language="ClickHouseSQL" implementationClass="dev.sort.clickhouse.catalog.ClickHouseReferencedSchemaIntrospector"/>
        <editorNotificationProvider implementation="dev.sort.clickhouse.catalog.ClickHouseIntrospectBannerProvider"/>
        <postStartupActivity implementation="dev.sort.clickhouse.catalog.ClickHouseExecutionObserverStartup"/>
        <notificationGroup id="ClickHouse catalog" displayType="BALLOON"/>
        <annotator language="ClickHouseSQL" implementationClass="dev.sort.clickhouse.pipe.ClickHouseStageAnnotator"/>
        <dynamicActionConfigurationCustomizer implementation="dev.sort.clickhouse.pipe.ClickHouseExecuteConfiguration"/>
        <dynamicActionConfigurationCustomizer implementation="dev.sort.clickhouse.ClickHouseStreamingCancelConfiguration"/>
        <actionPromoter implementation="dev.sort.clickhouse.pipe.ClickHouseExecutePromoter" order="first"/>
        <projectConfigurable id="dev.sort.clickhouse.pipe" displayName="ClickHouse PIPE" parentId="database.main" nonDefaultProject="true" instance="dev.sort.clickhouse.pipe.ClickHousePipeConfigurable"/>
        <notificationGroup id="ClickHouse PIPE" displayType="BALLOON"/>
        <intentionAction>
            <language>ClickHouseSQL</language>
            <className>dev.sort.clickhouse.pipe.ClickHousePreviewIntention</className>
            <category>ClickHouse</category>
        </intentionAction>
        <intentionAction>
            <language>ClickHouseSQL</language>
            <className>dev.sort.clickhouse.pipe.ClickHouseRunToStageIntention</className>
            <category>ClickHouse</category>
        </intentionAction>
    </extensions>
    <extensions defaultExtensionNs="com.intellij.database">
        <dbms id="CLICKHOUSE_BRIKK" instance="dev.sort.clickhouse.ClickHouseDbms.CLICKHOUSE_BRIKK"/>
        <extensionFallback dbms="CLICKHOUSE_BRIKK" fallbackDbms="CLICKHOUSE"/>
        <dialect dbms="CLICKHOUSE_BRIKK" implementationClass="com.intellij.database.dialects.clickhouse.CHouseDialect"/>
        <modelFacade dbms="CLICKHOUSE_BRIKK" implementationClass="com.intellij.database.dialects.clickhouse.model.CHouseModelFacade"/>
        <introspector dbms="CLICKHOUSE_BRIKK" implementationClass="dev.sort.clickhouse.ClickHouseIntrospectorFactory"/>
        <definitionProvider dbms="CLICKHOUSE_BRIKK" implementationClass="dev.sort.clickhouse.catalog.ClickHouseDefinitionProvider"/>
        <driversConfig config="config/clickhouse-drivers.xml"/>
        <connectionInterceptor implementation="dev.sort.clickhouse.catalog.ClickHouseHarvestConnectionInterceptor"/>
    </extensions>
    <actions>
        <action id="ClickHouse.RefreshCatalog" class="dev.sort.clickhouse.catalog.ClickHouseRefreshCatalogAction"
                text="Refresh ClickHouse Catalog" description="Read function names from the connected ClickHouse system catalog">
            <add-to-group group-id="EditorPopupMenu" anchor="last"/>
        </action>
        <group id="ClickHousePipe.EditorMenu" class="com.intellij.ide.actions.NonEmptyActionGroup" text="ClickHouse PIPE" popup="true">
            <add-to-group group-id="EditorPopupMenu" anchor="first"/>
            <action id="ClickHousePipe.Preview" class="dev.sort.clickhouse.pipe.ClickHousePreviewAction" text="Preview Generated SQL"/>
            <action id="ClickHousePipe.RunToStage" class="dev.sort.clickhouse.pipe.ClickHouseRunToStageAction" text="Run Stages up to Caret"/>
        </group>
    </actions>
    <applicationListeners>
        <listener class="dev.sort.clickhouse.catalog.ClickHouseLiveCatalogCleanup"
                  topic="com.intellij.database.dataSource.DataSourceStorage$Listener"/>
        <listener class="dev.sort.clickhouse.validation.ClickHouseVerificationConnectionListener"
                  topic="com.intellij.database.dataSource.DatabaseConnectionManager$Listener"/>
    </applicationListeners>
    <projectListeners>
        <listener class="dev.sort.clickhouse.catalog.ClickHouseLiveCatalogCleanup"
                  topic="com.intellij.database.dataSource.DataSourceStorage$Listener"/>
    </projectListeners>
</idea-plugin>
